WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.779
Whether you're unclear as to how all the pieces
of Netflix's new hit show Locke &amp; Key fit

00:00:04.779 --> 00:00:08.800
together, you want answers to some of its
bigger questions, or you're simply hankering

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:12.340
for some hints as to where season two might
head… this is what you need to know.

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:14.820
First thing's first: At the end of the day,
Dodge won.

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.920
Dodge's real goal wasn't stealing the Omega
Key.

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:19.060
It was opening the Black Door.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:21.760
She didn't need the Omega Key to accomplish
that.

00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:26.160
She simply had to trick Tyler, Kinsey, and
Bode into opening the door for her… which

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.020
they do, despite Kinsey's eventual better
judgment.

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:30.940
"Does this feel right to you?"

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:36.560
"If you have any better ideas, I'm all ears."

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:38.400
"Best available idea doesn't make something
a good idea."

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:43.490
Dodge's scheme isn't shown on screen chronologically,
so here's roughly how it works: First, Dodge

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:46.580
uses the Identity Key to transform Ellie into,
well…

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.280
Dodge.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.800
Then she straight-up knocks her out.

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:53.620
Next, Dodge uses the Crown of Shadows to summon
an army and leads an attack on Keyhouse.

00:00:53.620 --> 00:00:55.500
While the stakes feel real, they're not.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.240
Dodge intends to let the kids win.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.340
Then she drops Ellie's body, disguised as
her own, where the children can find it.

00:01:01.350 --> 00:01:05.630
In order to dispose of Dodge for good, Tyler,
Kinsey, and Bode need to put her back in the

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:06.180
Wellhouse.

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.340
Unfortunately, no one knows where Ellie hid
the Echo Key, so instead, the kids decide

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.760
to open the Black Door using the Omega Key
and dump Dodge inside.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:14.760
See where this is going?

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:18.700
The children and their friends throw Ellie's
disguised body through the portal even as

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:20.740
one of Dodge's demonic peers escape.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:24.960
Dodge's biggest threat, Ellie, is gone, her
other enemies think she's no longer part of

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:29.390
the equation, and now she has an equally powerful
and hungry partner in crime to help out.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:32.020
The Lockes think they won, but Dodge got everything
she wanted.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:35.900
Of course, getting rid of Ellie and opening
the Black Door isn't the only way that Dodge

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.380
has set herself up for success in season two.

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.440
As the final moments of Locke &amp; Key's first
season reveal, she's also earned Kinsey's

00:01:42.450 --> 00:01:47.210
trust and her heart by using the Identity
Key to masquerade as Gabe, a member of Kinsey's

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:47.800
friend group.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.180
As the season-closing montage implies, Dodge
has been masquerading as Gabe since the very

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:52.680
beginning.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.100
It was Dodge in the lobster suit.

00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:57.220
It was Dodge who tortured Eden using the Music
Box Key.

00:01:57.229 --> 00:01:59.460
It was Dodge who stole Kinsey away from Scot.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:00.140
That tracks.

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:04.560
Gabe doesn't appear until after Bode gives
Dodge the Anywhere Key in the first episode,

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.010
and his pitch-perfect emotional manipulation
of Kinsey always felt a little predatory.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:13.100
The Dodge-Gabe deception echoes one of the
graphic novel's main plotlines, although it

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:14.450
works a little differently in the book.

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.820
The Identity Key doesn't exist in the comics.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.360
Instead, Dodge uses the super straightforwardly
named Gender Key to switch between her male

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.300
and female forms.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:27.160
Masquerading as a boy named Zack, the male
Dodge who looks exactly like Ellie's old boyfriend,

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:30.320
Lucas becomes Tyler's best friend and Kinsey's
boyfriend.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.660
Expect something similar to follow in season
two.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:37.360
Still, it's not like Tyler, Kinsey, and Bode
ended Locke &amp; Key season one on a completely

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.060
down note.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.020
While they might've been duped into a false
sense of security, they did grow immensely

00:02:42.020 --> 00:02:45.410
thanks to their adventures in Keyhouse, and
were finally able to get over the death of

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:46.440
their dad, Rendell Locke.

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:50.000
When Locke &amp; Key begins, Tyler blames himself
for Rendell's murder.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:53.981
When Tyler's former classmate, Sam Lesser,
makes a crack about offing his father, Tyler

00:02:53.981 --> 00:02:56.100
jokingly asks Sam to kill Rendell, too.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:03:00.120
When Sam actually does murder Rendell, Tyler
can't help but feel responsible.

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:04.620
Meanwhile, Kinsey can't forgive herself for
being too afraid to fight Sam during the attack.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.880
Ultimately, Bode's trauma is a lot more simple:
He just misses his dad.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.280
"I wanna see my dad… please."

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:22.340
However, after Sam visits Keyhouse and reveals
that he's in league with Dodge, Tyler realizes

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.180
that Rendell's death had nothing to do with
him.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:28.420
Kinsey copes with her shame by literally dragging
her fear from her head and trying to kill

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:28.920
it.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.580
She only forgives herself once Tyler points
out that she wasn't able to stop Sam because

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.480
she was too busy protecting Bode.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:38.450
The youngest Locke sibling is now connected
to Rendell's legacy through Keyhouse and the

00:03:38.450 --> 00:03:41.070
magic keys, which Rendell also used as a boy.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:45.150
The loss of Rendell will always be a big factor
in the kids' lives, but as the season concludes,

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:47.500
they're also, finally, able to move forward.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.600
"Your house is filled with amazing keys.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:55.900
There's a key that can let you step outside
your body and be a ghost…"

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:56.520
"Whoa!"

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:57.900
"...And another that can change the way you
look."

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:00.900
One big mystery that Locke &amp; Key's first season
leaves hanging is the keys' true nature.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:04.080
We know they're magic, but why are they in
Keyhouse, and where did they come from?

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:08.540
If Locke &amp; Key continues to stick to the comic
books' mythology, we can find the answer there,

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.170
too: Quite simply, the keys are made out of
the bodies of the Children of Leng a race

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:13.780
of demons straight out of H.P.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:17.440
Lovecraft's playbook and were forged by the
Lockes' ancestors in order to control the

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.900
forces beyond the Black Door.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.460
In the comics, when a Child of Leng comes
out of the Black Door, they don't just die

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.880
when they fail to find a host.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:27.000
They actually turn into a substance known
as Whispering Iron.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.150
When Benjamin Locke discovered the Black Door
during the Revolutionary War, he quickly realized

00:04:31.150 --> 00:04:34.960
how dangerous it was and used the Whispering
Iron to make the Omega Key, keeping the door

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:35.460
shut.

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:39.460
Benjamin went on to make a number of other
keys, which he hid around Keyhouse for later

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:40.680
generations to find.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:44.820
Again, later seasons of the Netflix show might
retcon or streamline this history a little

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.990
bit, but the show's been faithful so far.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:48.700
It doesn't seem likely to change too much.

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.000
Even for comic book readers, it's hard to
tell exactly where Netflix's Locke &amp; Key is

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:53.520
headed.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:57.740
The first season burned through lots of the
comics' major plot points at a pretty rapid

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.580
pace, leaving the future very murky.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.400
Still, there are a few things we know.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.480
We haven't seen all of Keyhouse's magic keys.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:08.250
Without giving too much away, keys like the
Animal Key, the Angel Key, the Owl Key, and

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.300
the Giant Key will look great on screen and
should be lots of fun.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:15.660
Duncan, the kids' friendly uncle, has very
little to do in season one, but plays a much

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:19.780
bigger role as the story progresses and if
you think Dodge is finished with Bode, just

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:20.280
wait.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.640
The little guy is in for a very, very rough
time.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.700
The show also raises new questions that the
comics never dealt with.

00:05:25.860 --> 00:05:27.760
Kinsey's fear is attacking her classmates.

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.000
How will the kids stop it?

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:31.330
Ellie isn't dead, she's just trapped beyond
the Black Door.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:34.520
Is her time on the show done, or will she
find a way back through?

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.280
There are a lot of loose ends to tie up.

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:38.380
Season two can't get here soon enough.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:38.960
Until then…

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:39.860
"Aloha!"

